Reset 4's pstore `console-ramoops-0` (the boot that ended in the batch-4 run-25 reset): its
head (boot banner, kernel command line) and its last 40 lines (the heartbeat up to the stop,
including the `freq=900000` field on every line). 929 lines, 103428 bytes total; md5
9da1a586250410bbfdf345b528b18fcb -- matches the full record described in reset4-findings.md.
The MAC on the command line is redacted; the full 929-line copy is not committed. Mounted
read-only (`mount -t pstore -o ro pstore /sys/fs/pstore`), copied, unmounted; nothing in pstore
was deleted.

